rid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:08:04-07:00","id":1397343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397255#post1397255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Golconda was as much a &quot;myth&quot; in 2e as Revised. KOTE attempted to make the gaining of enlightenment, the transformation into an alien monster thing more front and center. That is the promise that I feel the Sabbat has fairly consistantly offered but failed at its all fiat. And if you are successful... you go leave the whole of kindred society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait what? KOTE doesn't have Golconda at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:21:23-07:00","id":1397347,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m personally not a big fan of Sabbat Paths and Wan Gui Dharmas being the same thing, but maybe I just need a little more convincing. I guess I could see an alliance of convenience between the Court of Infinite Thunders and the Gehenna Crusade if the Court tried to expand west into Persia and Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> Random question for anyone who knows: Is it a problem that the word Dharma is an Indian Buddhist concept but most of the Wan Gui (at least those of the Quincunx) are of Chinese ancestry and culture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:22:01-07:00","id":1397348,"title":"","content":"Maybe change Dharma to Dao (Tao)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:24:05-07:00","id":1397349,"title":"","content":"Alot of Indian and Chinese culture diffuse alot among eachother (discounting modern hostilities of today however). Buddhism most especially if I remember correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:46:11-07:00","id":1397354,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> that\u2019s a very good point. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T14:32:41-07:00","id":1397380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397343#post1397343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait what? KOTE doesn't have Golconda at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>it does,<br /> in fact, it originated from them<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397347#post1397347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m personally not a big fan of Sabbat Paths and Wan Gui Dharmas being the same thing, but maybe I just need a little more convincing.</div> </div> </div> </div>no need for convincing, since no one said they were the same thing<br /> <br /> I assume Lian's point has something to do with the bit of lore that claims cainites may take on a dharma,<br /> there's Saulot's story and the rumors in one of the kote books about some salubri that have managed to refine their beasts into p'o making them into pseudo kuei-jin on dharmas<br /> <br /> from there, you can theorize sabbat (which are already on alternative moralities) espousing the kj ways","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-18-2020, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T15:14:53-07:00","id":1397392,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhh<br /> <br /> Sabbat following Saulot and adopting the Dharmas of the Wan Gui as alternative Paths. Yeah, I guess that would be kinda cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T16:26:25-07:00","id":1397402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397347#post1397347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random question for anyone who knows: Is it a problem that the word Dharma is an Indian Buddhist concept but most of the Wan Gui (at least those of the Quincunx) are of Chinese ancestry and culture?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the huge influence of Buddhism on Chinese thought for the past couple of millennia, including on native Chinese religions like Daoism, and how its terminology still influences new religious movements like Falun Gong, it\u2019s not that weird. It\u2019s actually a rare aspect of KotE that\u2019s <i>not </i>cringeworthy from the perspective of someone familiar with the cultures in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:03:30-07:00","id":1397419,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> thank you. Really appreciate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:28:28-07:00","id":1397427,"title":"","content":"Mechanically I have always treated Golconda as behaving more like the KOTE dharmas (works out better that way IMHO) but in a larger (narrative/role playing) sense I don't worry too much about the details. I still treat Golconda as a personal effort at finding some sort of balance between the physical/metaphysical nature of the character, but how that is arrived at can be highly variable and could differ by region, culture, beliefs or a combination of other factors. The Dharmas are one way to do it, trying to cling to humanity might be another... but that doesn't mean OTHERS couldn't exist (including some possibly 'not good guy' ones, since as I recall that as one of the changes between earlier editions and revised.)<br /> <br /> So could you have some 'enlightened' Sabbat who might follow some Path and achieve some sort of spiritual discovery? Yeah I think you could, if its handled right by the player. But how it is handled is up to the skills of the player and storyteller more than anything.<br /> <br /> But it's also worth noting the political aspects here. The possibility that the Sabbat are being used for some larger scheme (by one faction or another in the Wan Kuei. Or the Sabbat, or both., Even if other factions of Wan Kuei ally with the Camarilla or even the Anarchs) can't be ignored either. I find it more likely any 'alliance' is driven by political rather than spiritual factors (the Sabbat is no more monolithic than the Wan Kuei are.) The Kindred are useful tools (and sometimes allies) at best to the WK, and garbage to be eradicated at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T02:15:09-07:00","id":1397475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397427#post1397427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it's also worth noting the political aspects here. The possibility that the Sabbat are being used for some larger scheme (by one faction or another in the Wan Kuei. Or the Sabbat, or both., Even if other factions of Wan Kuei ally with the Camarilla or even the Anarchs) can't be ignored either. I find it more likely any 'alliance' is driven by political rather than spiritual factors (the Sabbat is no more monolithic than the Wan Kuei are.) The Kindred are useful tools (and sometimes allies) at best to the WK, and garbage to be eradicated at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>unlikely for the sabbat to be used as tools,<br /> v5 has been shying away from the concept,<br /> <br /> Anarchs used to be camarilla tools...not anymore<br /> sabbat used to be lasombra tools...not anymore<br /> <br /> they also retconned wk territories into camarilla ones,<br /> so, just like for the sabbat, they wouldn't have a political structure anymore<br /> <br /> instead, the sabbat and kj would be merged into one group of terrorists","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T05:16:34-07:00","id":1397955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397256#post1397256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, it was at least real in 2nd Edition when Rebekah had it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> back when Mages could cure the curse of caine and let you keep all your cool vampire powers but none of the weaknesses. Suffice to say I'm not a big fan of Npc exceptionalism driving PC goals? The attainability for Golconda for pcs has always been debatable and even if it was the case of it being an all or nothing end of game event rather than something broken up into pieces showing growth over time.<br /> <br /> I would even argue that Golconda probably should be harder on Humanity given that Humanity is fundimentally static in nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397343#post1397343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait what? KOTE doesn't have Golconda at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>KJ enlightenment(and Coils of the Dragon in Requiem) are two ways to make Golconda more accessable in game. It pieces out self discovery and enlightenment into chunks that show up over time rather than the all or nothing setup.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397380#post1397380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I assume Lian's point has something to do with the bit of lore that claims cainites may take on a dharma,<br /> there's Saulot's story and the rumors in one of the kote books about some salubri that have managed to refine their beasts into p'o making them into pseudo kuei-jin on dharmas<br /> <br /> from there, you can theorize sabbat (which are already on alternative moralities) espousing the kj ways</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not suggesting the Sabbat suddenly be on the Dharmas of Xue. But rather the Sabbat return from their Crusade with some secrets that make them closer to WK. With alien moralities that functionally allow them transform their state overtime. We know much of the Cainite religion has been striped from them with the church of caine. So they need something to different than the various blood god cults we already have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T05:22:06-07:00","id":1397957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397955#post1397955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">back when Mages could cure the curse of caine and let you keep all your cool vampire powers but none of the weaknesses. Suffice to say I'm not a big fan of Npc exceptionalism driving PC goals? The attainability for Golconda for pcs has always been debatable and even if it was the case of it being an all or nothing end of game event rather than something broken up into pieces showing growth over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, they flat out canonized it and gave rules for it in STATE OF GRACE I believe.<br /> <br /> Which is about time.<br /> <br /> Golconda should be real, attainable, and not a myth, IMHO. That's just my campaign, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T05:40:48-07:00","id":1397960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397955#post1397955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not suggesting the Sabbat suddenly be on the Dharmas of Xue. But rather the Sabbat return from their Crusade with some secrets that make them closer to WK. With alien moralities that functionally allow them transform their state overtime. We know much of the Cainite religion has been striped from them with the church of caine. So they need something to different than the various blood god cults we already have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the church of caine was taken from the sabbat,<br /> the church of caine is an alternative take on noddism, inspired by the cainite heresy<br /> <br /> the sabbat noddism is just one of several takes on the faith,<br /> <br /> the path of Caine is an assamite take, similar to the path of blood, in which the faithful seek to get closer to caine through diablerie<br /> <br /> the path of power focuses on the defiant aspect of Caine, and his thirst for temporal power<br /> <br /> the cainite heresy, however, sees Caine as not cursed by god but a spiritual being blessed by god (and cursed by the demiurge),<br /> and his cainite descendents as angels on earth and the remaining spiritual beings on earth (while mortals are lowly demiurgic spawn)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T05:59:13-07:00","id":1397965,"title":"","content":"The Church of Caine sounds very Gnostic.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> is State of Grace any good? What else does it talk about besides Golconda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T06:06:56-07:00","id":1397967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397965#post1397965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Church of Caine sounds very Gnostic.</div> </div> </div> </div>it is 100% gnostic,<br /> it has its own take on abrahmaic religions,<br /> it claims Jesus as being Caine,<br /> and the expected return of the christ to be the return of Caine for the second time to free them from the demiurge<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is State of Grace any good? What else does it talk about besides Golconda? </div> </div> </div>it talks about religion in Vampire society,<br /> it's a decent read, but don't expect much in ways of gameplay mechanics<br /> <br /> I imagine cult of the blood gods is an attempt to address the lack of commitement in Sins of the Blood and State of Grace","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-21-2020, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T06:08:21-07:00","id":1397968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396507-wan-kuei-the-sabbat-and-the-gehenna-crusade?p=1397960#post1397960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the church of caine was taken from the sabbat,<br /> the church of caine is an alternative take on noddism, inspired by the cainite heresy<br /> <br /> the sabbat noddism is just one of several takes on the faith,<br /> <br /> the path of Caine is an assamite take, similar to the path of blood, in which the faithful seek to get closer to caine through diablerie<br /> <br /> the path of power focuses on the defiant aspect of Caine, and his thirst for temporal power<br /> <br /> the cainite heresy, however, sees Caine as not cursed by god but a spiritual being blessed by god (and cursed by the demiurge),<br /> and his cainite descendents as angels on earth and the remaining spiritual beings on earth (while mortals are lowly demiurgic spawn)</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this is revisions and retcons but basically:<br /> <br /> * The<b> Church of Caine </b>is a Astaru-esque revival of the original <b>Cainite Heresy</b>. They found the documents and rebuilt the church despite all members being dead.<br /> <br /> * The<b> Road of Heaven </b>was originally known as Noddism.<br /> <br /> * Sabbat noddism is a bastardized version of the Church of Caine that stole many of its ritae and teachings then shifted them under the <b>Lasombra</b> (who annihilated the Cainite Heresy in the first place)<br /> <br /> * The <b>Path of Caine </b>was created by <b>Dastur Anosh</b> who was a failed follower of the Path of Blood and basically rewrote the Path of Blood for the Sabbat. There's a very cynical take that the Path of Caine was taught the Sabbat by Assamite Antitribu because they were disgusted at the idea of teaching non-Assamites the Path of Blood, so they gave them a bastardized &quot;fake&quot; version of it. Dastur seems a sincere believer, though.<br /> <br /> * The <b>Path of Power and the Inner Voice </b>is a bastardized version of Lasombra teachings that were originally the<b> Road of Night</b>. However, weirdly, the<b> Path of Night </b>is NOTHING like the Road of Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T06:20:19-07:00","id":1397972,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> thanks. That\u2019s really helpful.<br /> <br /> I think imma hold off on State of Grace. I don\u2019t want to get confused by stuff that was in Revised